ent":"tome","entry_revision_identity":"30b3d62c92c3f11b928ae0392072f8e383f20cc3209722adca95486c024fe803","logical_entry_identity":"eef53110200030db5f4ccfc8d51c683900a8509bf6bacc5bca44d9c5d3f8e300","normalized_path":"mod-tome.lua","source":"#LIGHT_BLUE# * +5 Strength, +2 Dexterity, +2 Constitution","source_tag":"_t","target":"#LIGHT_BLUE# * +5 力量，+2 敏捷，+2 体质"},{"args_order":null,"call_locator":"8a438c1cc7a025808d66d5d0dbbd1a7cc078d3fac30788010b6103f8f97e5344","component":"tome","entry_revision_identity":"30b74c04f54f7e0253a9374fbd15d9e248867b546d1a5b59985785770364694b","logical_entry_identity":"9139e003ed61e80c5f781e56f3767dad767a75b2ad2f86f0b3d86d46678b6314","normalized_path":"mod-tome.lua","source":"Engulf yourself in a surge of mana, quickly restoring %d mana every turn for 10 turns.\n\t\tThe mana restored will increase with your Spellpower.","source_tag":"tformat","target":"将自己包围在法力的河水中，每回合回复 %d 点法力值，持续 10 回合。\n\t\t法力回复受法术强度加成。"},{"args_order":null,"call_locator":"6a50398cef63d84cead3a7a4f851e7a90d0dc040703289203f7c8393882037e5","component":"tome","entry_revision_identity":"30b9ddfd08e967b6b9d4e6539d540bba2bebe2d7edab0c9088842c32a881efef","logical_entry_identity":"53781298ddfaf8238fc43bb319a18bcb088ea9c31488728414bc1e1b00a2ae35","normalized_path":"mod-tome.lua","source":"stat","source_tag":"_t","target":"属性"},{"args_order":null,"call_locator":"9640ac6b1894479434538049669b6b6329b0fda50009d91e9bdb8e7bf6ec1120","component":"tome","entry_revision_identity":"30bb4b74ce17640e428fe70cbd518a0bff921a847fe3730f9d099b6f4ee5d4de","logical_entry_identity":"bedc0bb3f52b6544aeb0c71d927a6c1cb263a27bc4b4feaa5005be962c9bcf11","normalized_path":"mod-tome.lua","source":"Ah, the legendary Sher'Tul! How any scholar does love to write about them. Indeed, the texts are many, but the facts are few, as so little is known about this crucible race. The most learned and factual academic on the subject is the renowned explorer and archaeologist Darwood Oakton, but he has alas been missing for several months at the time of writing. I will attempt to summarise here some of his key discoveries.\n\nThe Sher'Tul lived over ten thousand years ago, during what is referred to as the Age of Haze. The name of the race we know from the elves, who speak of the ancient beings with awe and reverence, yet know little else about them. Ruins of fantastical Sher'Tul structures have been found all across Maj'Eyal, and some have been observed in sunken lands off the coasts, implying that in their time the Sher'Tul must have ruled unopposed all across the world.\n\nThe farportals were first discovered by the halflings during the Age of Allure, and after much experimentation they were found to be able to transport items and creatures over vast distances. The arcane powers behind these incredible artifacts are still far beyond the understanding of the greatest minds of our time. The one attempt to truly tap into these powers ended in disaster - the Shaloren moved all known farportals to a remote spot near their capital, and their most powerful mages were overwhelmed as they unleashed the Spellblaze, killing them instantly and tearing apart the continent. What remains of farportals are left in the world have since been left untouched.\n\nOf their physical appearance we know almost nothing, as there is no surviving artwork or records which depict themselves. However they must have been of similar form to other common races, as their ruins contain stairs, doorways and rooms not unfit for humans. Oakton estimates from his studies of their tools and artifacts that they would have stood around 5'4\" tall, with uncommonly long limbs and fingers.\n\nWhat caused them to become extinct is unknown, though many theories abound. The most popular in academic circles at the moment is that their mighty magics were their undoing, turned upon their own people during some great civil strife. Other theories hold weight though - Archiman Garybald, Professor of Demonic Studies, believes that the extensive uses of arcane energies by the Sher'Tul may have attracted twisted forces from other worlds which wiped out the ancient race. Some even believe that they are not truly extinct, but are in hiding, or have left this world for elsewhere. I fear the truth may never be fully known, but the ongoing study and examination of the relics they have left behind continues to provide immense value and inspiration.","source_tag":"_t","target":"啊，传奇的夏·图尔！学者们是多么爱研究他们啊。事实上，相关的文献很多，但有事实根据的很少，所以有关该种族的信息也较少。最权威的研究是基于知名探险家和考古学家达沃德·欧卡顿的发现，但是他在写作过程中已经失踪好几个月了。在此，我将总结下他关键性的几个发现。\n\n夏·图尔生活在距今一万年前，被称为混沌纪的时代。这个种族的名字来源于精灵族，他们以敬畏之情述说着古代种族，即便如此，他们也对其知之甚少。在马基·埃亚尔大陆上，夏·图尔如梦似幻的废墟结构被找出并探索，有的废墟甚至位于海洋中沉没的大陆上，暗示着夏·图尔人曾经一度统治过整个世界。\n\n传送门的首次发现是在厄流纪，被半身人发现，在大量的实验后他们发现可以将物品和生物传送到很远的地方。这些奇迹背后的奥术原理仍远远超出我们能够理解的范围。那些试图刨根挖底的人，现在湮灭在了历史中——那些永恒精灵法师将所有已知的传送门搬到了一个靠近他们首都的地方，并且他们的法师被释放出的能量所淹没，从而引发了魔法大爆炸，他们瞬间化为了灰烬并且整个大陆分崩离析。那些在大陆上剩下的传送门，至今无人敢碰。\n\n关于他们的长相几乎没有人说得清，因为毫无历史文献或者是记录来描述他们的样子。然而他们肯定与其他种族有着类似的特征，因为他们的废墟中存在着适合人类的楼梯、门廊和房间。欧卡顿通过研究他们的工具和遗迹，得出了这样的结论：他们大约高5英尺4英寸左右，有着异常修长的四肢和手指。\n\n他们绝迹的原因始终是个未解之谜，尽管有着各种猜想。在考古界最流行的说法是他们强大的魔法毁灭了自己，内战使他们消弭在历史中。其他理论——阿奇曼·加里伯德，恶魔研究者则一直相信夏·图尔人在魔法上的杰出造诣引来了异次元的恶魔，最终导致了整个种族的毁灭。有的人则更相信他们不是真的绝迹了，而是隐匿了起来，或者离开了这个世界。我恐怕真相永远无人知晓，但是对夏·图尔文明的深入研究仍有着非常重要的价值和意义。"},{"args_order":null,"call_locator":"fe1c3848074d6acdfbe489f93c765281cdb85c7e720ba6354900c7b6c08876a8","component":"tome","entry_revision_identity":"30be8469c65aaf012acbdf30199a5933671930713ead5814989225e4b8550896","logical_entry_identity":"da792f61769b99374a72fbb865e4d724744d922329bb24f257f63a511ecbbb4a","normalized_path":"mod-tome.lua","source":"Hidden compound","source_tag":"_t","target":"隐藏的竞技场"},{"args_order":null,"call_locator":"44555596f11dde87e459edc8a93c775fdc99857caec0a1f892588ed25cdb481f","component":"tome","entry_revision_identity":"30c00effdf422054e3b6836f7dcdbc27f2a3683d16df673b797a08dc7e883685","logical_entry_identity":"0e30fba7d069fde06dc58c3ea4f40303eb9687edaccca9fb241daa1a53913ad4","normalized_path":"mod-tome.lua","sourc